Package: notesci
Version: __VERSION__
Section: web
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: notesci maintainers <noreply@notesci.com>
Homepage: https://notesci.com
Depends: postgresql (>= 16),
 postgresql-16-pgvector,
 python3.12,
 python3.12-venv,
 libwebkit2gtk-4.1-0,
 libsoup-3.0-0,
 libayatana-appindicator3-1,
 librsvg2-2,
 adduser,
 ca-certificates
Description: Personal knowledge base for scientific research
 notesci is a single-user, self-hosted research workspace that grounds
 chat responses in your own corpus of papers and notes. It speaks to
 multiple LLM providers (Anthropic, OpenAI, Google, DeepSeek) through
 one chokepoint and hosts MCP servers for tools you bring yourself.
 .
 This package installs notesci as a native desktop application. The
 Tauri-built binary at /opt/notesci/bin/notesci spawns the Python
 backend on launch and embeds the React frontend in a native window
 (via WebKitGTK). Configuration lives in /etc/notesci/notesci.conf.
 .
 After install, launch "notesci" from your application menu.
